  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "bo_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -324
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Breakout\n\nClick the preview to start, then move the mouse left and right to steer the paddle; click again to launch each ball. Break every brick to go up a level (the ball gets faster); three balls, then click to play again. Until you click, the game plays itself.\n\nHow it works: the game is state — the ball's position and velocity, which bricks are still standing (a State* of 60), score, lives, level. Every frame one Expression moves the ball, another tests it against all 60 bricks at once (per element over the brick spread), and the velocity Expression bounces it off the walls, the paddle (where it lands steers it) and any brick it hit. Sparks fly from broken bricks.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 260
      }
    },
